{"sequence":14,"timestamp":"2026-03-30T06:01:44.284253968Z","event_type":"amendment_queued","details":{"amendment_id":"fr-1-5075c6ab","body":"Add validation for `chloride_protection_factor` in `validate_shrimp_runtime_params()` (invariants.rs). Currently `critical_molt_gh_ratio`, `molt_success_threshold`, and all other named shrimp parameters are validated, but `chloride_protection_factor` has no bounds check. A negative or NaN value would silently break the hazard formula (the `.max(0.0)` inside `compute_effective_nitrite_hazard` handles negatives at runtime, but NaN/Infinity would propagate). Add `check_non_negative(\"shrimp_params.chloride_protection_factor\", params.chloride_protection_factor)?;` alongside the existing parameter checks, and add a corresponding invalid-value test case to the `malformed_current_save_with_invalid_molt_mineral_parameters_is_rejected` and `step_hours_rejects_invalid_molt_mineral_parameters_before_simulation` tests.","dedup_key":"f7a7b4820691855d3ead85d32dfd5630b1fd18926f6dba5ef109bd512e2a0d50","run_id":"run-20260330051540","source":"workflow_stage","source_stage":"final_review"}}
