{"sequence":30,"timestamp":"2026-03-30T06:35:05.245804207Z","event_type":"amendment_queued","details":{"amendment_id":"fr-2-2792298a","body":"Add invariant enforcement for `denitrifier_activity_index` in `invariants.rs:enforce_invariants`. All other 0–1 indices (`biofilter_maturity_index`, `maturity_index`, `nuisance_index`, etc.) are clamped in `enforce_invariants` (lines 21–49), but `denitrifier_activity_index` is not. A corrupted save or deserialization of an out-of-range value (e.g., > 1.0) would propagate unchecked into the denitrification rate calculation at `nitrogen_cycle.rs:537`, amplifying the denitrification rate beyond the intended ceiling.","dedup_key":"75f103c02600ced6893391295ddf324ba006e0a24422fe7680850bfd99aebd9e","run_id":"run-20260330051540","source":"workflow_stage","source_stage":"final_review"}}
{"sequence":31,"timestamp":"2026-03-30T06:35:05.255751789Z","event_type":"amendment_queued","details":{"amendment_id":"fr-2-e08fb6f7","body":"Add `check_non_negative` invariant validation for `cumulative_n2_export_mg_n` in `invariants.rs:validate_invariants_inner`. This field is a monotonically increasing cumulative counter (only incremented at `nitrogen_cycle.rs:570`) and is part of the nitrogen budget array (`budget.rs`). A negative value from a corrupted save would silently unbalance the nitrogen budget without any diagnostic error.","dedup_key":"06bde2fb51686f6911edb33ff9670c38f4fb94e2f7f929ec94beff64de1222a3","run_id":"run-20260330051540","source":"workflow_stage","source_stage":"final_review"}}
{"sequence":32,"timestamp":"2026-03-30T06:35:05.265641121Z","event_type":"amendment_queued","details":{"amendment_id":"fr-2-8f4f8117","body":"Add `check_non_negative` invariant validation for the five new denitrification process params (`denitrification_vmax_mg_n_per_l_per_hour`, `denitrification_k_no3_mg_n_per_l`, `denitrification_k_doc_mg_c_per_l`, `denitrification_pore_water_mixing_factor`, `denitrification_activity_maturation_days`) in the process params validation block at `invariants.rs:220–288`. The code applies `.max(0.01)` and `safe_rate()` defensively at the call site (`nitrogen_cycle.rs:531–538`), but all other kinetic process params (aob_vmax, nob_vmax, decomposer_vmax, etc.) are validated up front in invariants. Missing this creates an inconsistency where invalid configs are silently clamped rather than rejected.","dedup_key":"27d3c47f71fb2a7a9c3353422d0607487e3875f7606bf4c4b3bceec89fff0c6a","run_id":"run-20260330051540","source":"workflow_stage","source_stage":"final_review"}}
{"sequence":33,"timestamp":"2026-03-30T06:35:05.275561332Z","event_type":"amendment_queued","details":{"amendment_id":"fr-2-e421d6bc","body":"Update the stale doc comment on `DENITRIFICATION_ALK_MEQ_PER_MG_N` in `process.rs:25–27` which still reads 'Reserved for E4b (denitrification implementation). When wiring, add...' — denitrification is now implemented and this constant is actively used at `nitrogen_cycle.rs:572`. The comment should reflect current usage rather than future intent.","dedup_key":"cdbeb3591cd44f4641c77621ac2399d1ca3bd58a955f862d77870739b361ed7a","run_id":"run-20260330051540","source":"workflow_stage","source_stage":"final_review"}}
